{
  "_about": [
    "Golden cases for the reaction lane frame and for how a lane of reactions folds into what a client shows.",
    "Normative: docs/sealed-messages.md §Reactions.",
    "The reactor is never in the payload: it is the MLS sender, read from the decrypted credential.",
    "Parsing is strict JSON (RFC 8259): an unquoted key, a single-quoted string, a trailing comma or a duplicate key (compared after unescaping, at any depth) makes the payload not a reaction. A first-wins and a last-wins reader would otherwise show different emoji for one frame.",
    "`call` names the question. `encode` gives a reaction, the exact keys the wire carries, and what parsing that wire back gives. `parse` gives a wire string and what a reader reads out of it, or null for anything that is not a valid reaction.",
    "`fold` gives a lane of {sender, wire} in mailbox order and the reactions a client shows: per sender, the latest valid frame for this message wins and a clear removes that sender's reaction. `draw` maps emoji to sender ids sorted ascending, with no empty lists.",
    "To replay: run each case through your own implementation of the format and compare the result with the case's expectation, field by field."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "encode/set",
      "why": "An ordinary reaction.",
      "call": "encode",
      "reaction": {
        "messageId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
        "emoji": "👍",
        "remove": false
      },
      "keys": [
        "e",
        "m",
        "peachy",
        "v"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "messageId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
        "emoji": "👍",
        "remove": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "encode/clear",
